00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:32.060
We shouldn't have meddled.

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:34.000
We shouldn't have meddled.

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:39.920
Do you hear that?

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:41.330
What is that?

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:42.900
Up!

00:17:42.900 --> 00:17:44.900
It's right outside the tent.

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:47.920
It's open!

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:49.880
I'm going outside the tent.

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.250
Something's outside.

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:57.200
But he's been in our backpacks!

00:17:57.200 --> 00:17:59.160
They ate our food!

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:02.520
Scooby Doo!

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:06.410
He he he he! Scooby Dooby Doo!

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:08.410
Thanks a lot Scooby!

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:12.170
Fred! Wake up!

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:14.910
Daphne? Daphne?

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:16.970
Freddy! There's something out there again!

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:18.820
Daphne!

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:21.120
God darn, it was just a dream.

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:27.780
What are we gonna do now, Velma?

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:30.000
There's no food, no clean clothes!

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:33.000
I haven't painted my nails in two days!

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:37.880
Shh! Did you hear that?

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:39.390
Hello?

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:46.930
Hello?

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:50.970
Gooby-doo?

00:18:50.970 --> 00:18:52.370
Is that you?

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:36.860
I suppose you think this is very funny.

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:39.360
I ruined my stockings.

00:19:39.730 --> 00:19:41.330
I hope you're happy, Scoob.

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:44.270
I just hope you're happy because I don't have another pair.

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:44.630
Shh.

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:46.450
I think I hear it again.

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:48.310
Uncle Scooby.

00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:51.950
Thanks.

00:19:54.220 --> 00:19:55.000
All lights off.

00:19:55.950 --> 00:19:58.080
What's he doing here?

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:00.000
Why did you call him Scoob?

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:03.480
- He probably wants to solve the mystery for us.

00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:04.840
He loves doing that.

00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:09.250
- Shh.

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:15.420
- Did you hear that?

00:20:15.420 --> 00:20:19.020
- Gang, looks like there's a mystery to be solved.

00:20:19.020 --> 00:20:21.430
- Hi, Scrappy.

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:24.450
- Wait till I get a hold of that monster, Uncle Scooby.

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:25.760
He'll never know what hit him.

00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:28.120
I'll give him one of those, and one of these.

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:30.000
And Uncle Scooby can give him one of these,

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:32.860
And one of those, won't ya Uncle Scooby, won't ya?

00:20:32.860 --> 00:20:34.560
Yeah, right Wappy?

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:37.060
I don't think Scooby needs any help, Scrappy.

00:20:37.060 --> 00:20:38.060
What do you mean, Freddy?

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:40.060
You guys haven't caught anybody yet?

00:20:40.060 --> 00:20:43.440
Now that I'm here, this mystery's gonna be wrapped up.

00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:44.940
It'll be solved before sunrise.

00:20:44.940 --> 00:20:46.940
That is, unless you chicken out, Freddy.

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:47.940
It's Fred.

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:49.940
There's only one thing you guys need.

00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:52.940
A good dose of puppy power!

00:20:52.940 --> 00:20:54.940
Oh yeah, that's just what we need.

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:59.890
Hey, it's that kooky creep. Let me at him.

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:04.460
Uncle Scooby, let's give him the old 1-4.

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:05.670
1-4?

00:21:05.670 --> 00:21:10.900
Well, gang?

00:21:10.900 --> 00:21:13.340
Well, what?

00:21:13.340 --> 00:21:14.520
Well...

00:21:14.520 --> 00:21:17.860
We better find the way out of here faster!

00:21:17.860 --> 00:21:21.980
Oh, man!

00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:23.980
Guys, I think I found something!

00:21:23.980 --> 00:21:24.980
What is it, Freddy?

00:21:24.980 --> 00:21:26.990
It looks like an abandoned drive-in.

00:21:26.990 --> 00:21:29.990
What would a drive-in be doing all the way out here?

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:32.350
I don't know, and I don't care!

00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:34.350
Just lead us to that snack bar!

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:36.270
Yeah! Snack bar!

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:40.270
Shaggy, that candy's gotta be at least 30 years old!

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:47.860
The noises are coming from this house!

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:50.740
Like, let's go in the haunted house in the middle of the night!

00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:52.820
Now I know why you're the smart one!

00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:55.640
Hello? Hello?

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:57.920
Hey, look! A radio!

00:21:57.920 --> 00:21:59.670
Maybe we're on the news!

00:22:04.990 --> 00:22:09.250
We always get changed when there's music!

00:22:30.350 --> 00:22:31.760
Ahh!

00:23:00.110 --> 00:23:02.070
Untie me, you intrusive kids.

00:23:02.330 --> 00:23:03.830
Like he didn't say meddling.

00:23:04.170 --> 00:23:05.230
Doesn't he know the drill?

00:23:05.710 --> 00:23:07.990
He used the costume to scare people.

00:23:08.310 --> 00:23:10.310
But one thing doesn't make sense.

00:23:10.670 --> 00:23:10.890
Why?

00:23:11.390 --> 00:23:12.470
Because it's Halloween.

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:15.500
October 31st, every year.

00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:18.220
Candy and Bobby for Apples.

00:23:18.300 --> 00:23:19.280
I mean, you guys are dressed up, right?

00:23:19.650 --> 00:23:22.960
But why did you scare us at the cemetery last night?

00:23:25.160 --> 00:23:28.380
Well, if you didn't do it, then who?

00:23:29.400 --> 00:23:30.000
Who?

00:23:41.550 --> 00:23:46.520
a dirt road. Search parties have spent several days searching the woods and found

00:23:46.520 --> 00:23:51.860
hundreds of scooby snacks but no trace of the teenage sluice have been found.

00:25:01.630 --> 00:25:03.790
You're watching Cartoon Network.
